{# THE WIDGET LIBRARY for the roster surface — chrome around the widget module's
   shared preset component.

   Nothing team-shaped happens inside that component: it is handed this
   surface's catalogue, this surface's partial name and this surface's routes,
   and it renders the strips, the toolbar and the canvas. Arranging a dashboard
   here works exactly as it does on every other surface in the installation,
   which is the whole reason this module rides the framework rather than
   carrying a copy of it. #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiShell/page.html.twig' %}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/team/_bits.html.twig' as bits %}

{% block title %}Matrix widgets{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiTeam/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_tabs %}{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ path('team_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> / <a href="{{ path('team_index') }}">team</a> / <a href="{{ path('team_positions') }}">positions</a> / widgets
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Matrix widgets{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}
    Six directions over one array &mdash; <code>PermissionCatalogue::groupedByUmbrella()</code> &mdash; plus the
    context that can ride any of them. Five of the six are ALTERNATIVES: keep exactly one on, because five
    renderings of one thing must not be able to disagree about it. Every card carries the direction&rsquo;s own
    trade-off line: what it buys, and what it costs.
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    <a class="tgl w-act" href="{{ path('team_positions') }}">{{ bits.icon_back() }} Back to the matrix</a>
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiWidget/widgets/_library.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}
